          "english": "Imagine sitting down to a big dinner: a massive steak, a large portion of fried potatoes, and cake for dessert. After eating so much, you should be too full to eat another bite. But some people experience a powerful urge to keep eating, even after __(26)__ in a huge meal, a behavior that makes little sense, as most adults are well-versed in the dangers of obesity, which researchers have shown correlates with __(27)__ health issues and is even linked to increased __(28)__ risk. But some people still keep eating long after they should stop, a phenomenon Dr. Susan Thompson calls \"insatiable(永不满足的) hunger.\" It is characterized by two main __(29)__ : not being satisfied by eating, and having a desire to stay sedentary(久坐不动的).",
          "chinese": "想象一下坐下来享用一顿丰盛的晚餐：一大块牛排、一大份炸土豆，还有蛋糕作为甜点。吃了这么多之后，你应该已经撑得一口也吃不下了。然而，有些人即使大吃了一顿，仍会产生继续进食的强烈冲动。这种行为似乎毫无道理，因为大多数成年人都十分了解肥胖的危害，而研究人员已经证明，肥胖与无数健康问题相关，甚至会增加死亡风险。但有些人即使早就应该停下，却仍然继续进食很久，这种现象被Susan Thompson博士称为“永不满足的饥饿”。它具有两个主要特征：进食后仍未感到满足，以及想要保持久坐不动的状态。",
